  "id": "assimilation",
  "term": "assimilation",
  "definition": "In this context, assimilation means hearing a speech sound from one language as matching or resembling a sound category from another language. It is used in speech perception research to study cross-linguistic phonetic similarity and how listeners may perceive second-language sounds.",
